// Benchmark 6 (`docs/rfc.md` §7.8): Lawful-void, unlawful-valid, and proved `Immunity ... Unless` triad.
//! explore: 1
Fact host Identified by Host1.
Fact tenant Identified by Tenant1.
Fact panel Identified by Panel1.
Fact quorum Identified by panel.
Fact emergency Identified by tenant.
Fact power-cut Identified by tenant.
Fact lease-terminated Identified by tenant.

// Unlawful physical act that still takes factual effect (`lawful = no, valid = yes`):
Act cut-power Actor host Recipient tenant
  Holds when emergency(tenant)
  Creates power-cut(tenant).

// Institutional power gated by `Valid when` and `Immunity` (`lawful = yes, valid = no` when immune):
Power terminate-lease Actor panel Recipient tenant
  Holds when True
  Valid when quorum(panel)
  Creates lease-terminated(tenant).

Immunity quiet-enjoyment Holder tenant
  Against terminate-lease
  Holds when True
  Unless emergency(tenant).

Invariant immune-tenant-not-terminated When (Forall tenant: emergency(tenant) When lease-terminated(tenant)).

+quorum(Panel1).

Scenario triad-orthogonality {
  // 1. Unlawful but factually effective:
  ?!lawful cut-power(Host1, Tenant1).
  ?valid cut-power(Host1, Tenant1).
  cut-power(Host1, Tenant1).
  ?power-cut(Tenant1).

  // 2. Lawful to propose, but void under quiet-enjoyment Immunity:
  ?lawful terminate-lease(Panel1, Tenant1).
  ?!valid terminate-lease(Panel1, Tenant1).
  terminate-lease(Panel1, Tenant1).
  ?!lease-terminated(Tenant1).

  // 3. Emergency lifts Unless condition -> both lawful and valid:
  +emergency(Tenant1).
  ?valid terminate-lease(Panel1, Tenant1).
  terminate-lease(Panel1, Tenant1).
  ?lease-terminated(Tenant1).
}
